## Prerequisites

```bash
# Update system
sudo apt update && sudo apt upgrade -y

# Install build tools
sudo apt install -y build-essential cmake git

# Install development libraries
sudo apt install -y libgpiod-dev libi2c-dev libspdlog-dev


###Setup Permissions

# Run setup script
sudo ./scripts/setup_permissions.sh

# Add user to required groups
sudo usermod -a -G gpio,i2c,dialout $USER


###scripts and tests provide

setup_permissions.sh - Configures system permissions, udev rules, groups, and kernel modules for all peripherals

configure_pins.sh - Interactive pin mux configuration tool for UART, SPI, I2C, PWM, and camera interfaces

test_all_peripherals.sh - Comprehensive test suite covering GPIO, UART, SPI, I2C, PWM, Ethernet, USB, PCIe, CAN, Camera, and M.2

test_gpio.cpp - Tests GPIO basic I/O, interrupts, and performance

test_uart.cpp - Tests UART communication, baud rates, async reads, and flow control

test_spi.cpp - Tests SPI transfers, modes, speeds, and ADC sensor

test_i2c.cpp - Tests I2C bus scanning, read/write, SMBus, and BME280 sensor

test_pwm.cpp - Tests PWM frequency, duty cycle, fading, servo control, and software PWM

###Examples:::
These 16 example files provide complete, working demonstrations for all peripherals:

    GPIO Examples: LED blinking, button input, interrupt handling

    UART Examples: Echo server, baud rate testing

    RS485 Examples: Modbus RTU master and slave implementations

    SPI Examples: Loopback test, ADC reading (MCP3008)

    I2C Examples: Bus scanner, BME280 sensor reading

    PWM Examples: Servo control, LED dimming with effects

    Ethernet Examples: UDP communication, TCP server/client

    CAN Examples: Frame reception and transmission

    Camera Examples: GStreamer pipeline, V4L2 direct capture

Each example includes detailed comments, error handling, and can be compiled and run directly on the Jetson Orin Nano.



